---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Slate Support | Slate"
  description="Help with Slate for Windows, browser capture, Quick Search, and Merge."
  home={false}
>
  <article class="shell privacy-page support-page">
    <p class="eyebrow">SLATE / SUPPORT</p>
    <h1>Slate Support</h1>
    <p class="privacy-intro">
      Help with installing Slate, saving from Chrome, and finding your clips.
    </p>
    <section>
      <h2>Getting started</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>
          Install <a href="/#download">Slate for Windows</a>.
        </li>
        <li>Install the Slate Chrome extension.</li>
        <li>
          Keep the Slate desktop app installed. Browser capture requires it.
        </li>
        <li>Save from Chrome to your local Slate library.</li>
      </ol>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2>Saving from Chrome</h2>
      <p>
        Select useful text, right-click, and choose{' '}
        <strong>Save selection</strong>. Use <strong>Save this page</strong> to
        keep the page's link and title. On supported ChatGPT, Claude, and Gemini
        pages, you can also use the selection's <strong>Save</strong> action.
      </p>
      <p>Source links and page context are retained where available.</p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2>Quick Search</h2>
      <p>
        Press{' '}
        <span class="support-shortcut">
          <kbd>Ctrl</kbd> + <kbd>Shift</kbd> + <kbd>Space</kbd>
        </span>{' '}
        while Slate is running to find saved clips without navigating the full
        library.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2>Merge</h2>
      <p>
        Select related clips and choose <strong>Merge</strong> to group them.
        The original clips stay separate, with each member's content, source and
        date accessible. Use <strong>Unmerge</strong> for an individual member
        or the whole group to return clips to the library.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2>Troubleshooting</h2>
      <h3>Browser capture is not appearing</h3>
      <p>
        Check that Slate is installed and running, and the Chrome extension is
        installed and enabled. Retry the capture. If needed, restart Slate and
        Chrome.
      </p>
      <h3>Quick Search does not open</h3>
      <p>
        Confirm Slate is running and retry Ctrl + Shift + Space. Restart Slate
        if it still does not open.
      </p>
      <h3>The extension cannot connect</h3>
      <p>
        The extension connects to the locally installed Slate desktop app. Check
        that both are installed, then restart Slate and Chrome.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2>Platform support</h2>
      <p>
        Slate is available for Windows 11 on Windows x64 (Intel and AMD) and
        Windows ARM64 PCs. Choose the installer for your device.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2>Reporting a problem</h2>
      <p>
        Visit
        <a
          href={site.repositoryUrl}
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          title="Open Slate on GitHub in a new tab"
        >
          Slate on GitHub
        </a>
        . Include what you tried, your Windows architecture, and the error
        message. Do not share private clip content.
      </p>
    </section>
    <a class="text-link" href="/">
      Back to Slate <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
    </a>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
